        "notes": "WARNING!!!! -  [Snowball Flight](item_770c6b61-98a8-489f-b44e-c1cc65c0cd7d) pushes you above the contesting height of most objectives. Keep this in mine\n\nFirst Major Transition. Here we pick up  [Snowball Flight](item_770c6b61-98a8-489f-b44e-c1cc65c0cd7d). As we begin to move towards AP, we are going to run a mixed WP/AP build.  [Icy Veins](item_2c403951-4f9b-4390-ad1e-aabaa09a6da5) is going to be a key piece of the build going forward, but is not immediately necessary.  You may consider  [Phantasmic Flux](item_5e644a79-cf6e-4196-8d0a-232f75004643) as an all-in-one perk that bridges the gap, but if your walls are getting value, Icy Veins is the way to go. You also get increased damage from overlapping blizzards.\n\nSide note: Avoid pushing for getting just a few epic perks. Rare and purple value primarily comes at worse rates. Focus on filling out your perks as much as you can for better value and upgrade to stronger perks as you can.\n\nPlaystyle: You have a very strong ability to box people in. For easy picks if your team is is helping. If they lack far back hitscan, really utilize walking on top of your\n\nWARNING!!!! -  [Snowball Flight](item_770c6b61-98a8-489f-b44e-c1cc65c0cd7d) pushes you above the contesting height of most objectives. Keep this in mind as you contest point and push into extended overtimes. \n\nSplurges: Buffs to Weapon Damage, Cooldown reduction, and Survivability but try to keep perks filled out\n\nAlternative considerations:  [Iridescent Iris](item_b7fb28ef-ce82-416b-8693-01c274f8df4e)",
