        "created_at": "2025-07-14T00:58:01.999893+00:00",
        "notes": "Power:  [Twice as Ice](item_f2bf9a0f-1a59-406a-bf9f-3b9c2abc2a84)\n\nHere is where the build really starts coming together.  [Twice as Ice](item_f2bf9a0f-1a59-406a-bf9f-3b9c2abc2a84) doesn't just \"reset\" Ice Wall and  [Snowball Flight](item_770c6b61-98a8-489f-b44e-c1cc65c0cd7d) pillars, it BANKS A CHARGE. This means that if you use Cryo in spawn or between fights, you effectively have 2 charges ready and a third the next time you use Cryo for a serious amount of pressure and blizzard AOE uptime.\n\nBecause of this, we no longer need cooldown reduction so we can drop  [Iridescent Iris](item_b7fb28ef-ce82-416b-8693-01c274f8df4e) and  [Multi-Tool](item_5ba8d94e-f2f3-44b7-8773-025fc6ed7c56) if you were running them.\n\nWe now have a HUGE amount of point presence and area control. Keep up ability lifesteal for survivability. If enemy damage is super high and survivability is an issue, consider  [Divine Intervention](item_b5148b7f-8529-4b1b-a90c-5d7cf13f8f0c) for burst damage and  [Ogundimu Reduction Field](item_b12daf48-069b-44c1-88fe-221cbcff664d) for sustained enemy damage.\n\nSubstitute power - if you choose to run  [Blizznado](item_208ab663-2529-489a-87d9-d798d94f4c22), definitely consider running  [Ice Sheet](item_6dd4ada0-3a27-4e54-b321-d67a1bf5790e) to boost wall uptime, especially if they are actively destroying pillars. Ice sheet is not necessary if you are running twice as ice, just replace the walls and pillars.",
